  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 1e0d8dd5b8f33e34b965fec3f1ff8d3e, type: 3}
  m_Name: L1809_InteractingOpenSpaceThrowsError
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  exerciseNumber: 09
  exerciseName: InteractingOpenSpaceThrowsError
  exerciseTitle: Interacting in open space throws Error
  videoWalkthroughUrl: https://unitycodemonkey.teachable.com/courses/problem-solving/lectures/63459447
  exerciseText: Interacting in empty space throws error
  hintText: Why is it only in empty space? Why does it not throw an error when near
    an Interactable object?
  solutionText: The code is not checking for null when calling the .Interact(); function
    which naturally throws an error if there are no nearby interactable objects.
